cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AstraX in research, teaching material or publications, please cite it as below."
title: "AstraX: an open-source spaceflight simulation laboratory"
type: software
version: 4.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/arshc0der/AstraX"
authors:
  - name: "Arsh and the AstraX contributors"
keywords:
  - spaceflight
  - orbital mechanics
  - rocket design
  - simulation
  - education
abstract: >-
  AstraX is a desktop simulation laboratory for rocket design, launch simulation, survival testing, orbit analysis and
  interplanetary launch-window planning. Results come from simplified, documented models and are not validated mission predictions.
